---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const pageTitle = 'About us';
---

<BaseLayout lang="en" pageTitle={pageTitle}>
	<article class="max-w-xl mx-auto relative flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
		<h1 class="title text-3xl bg-gradient-to-r from-accent-two/85 via-accent-one/85 to-accent-two/85 dark:from-accent-two dark:via-accent-one dark:to-accent-two bg-clip-text text-transparent">Voting Abroad</h1>

		<section class="w-full mt-6">
			<h2 class="title mb-4 text-xl text-accent-two">Why it matters to register and vote</h2>
			<p>
				Although Serbia is, by its constitution, a democratic republic, in reality it has long been governed by an autocratic regime that disregards the rule of law. One major consequence is the consistent manipulation of elections, with increasing evidence of fraud in each cycle.
			</p>
			<p>
				Despite these manipulations, parliamentary elections remain the only legal means of changing this corrupt regime, and we hope this will eventually lead to the fulfillment of students' demands.
			</p>
			<p>
				A key manipulation tactic is the opaque management of the electoral roll, which lacks public oversight and includes parallel databases. Diaspora voters, who are physically absent but formally present in the system, are an ideal target for abuse.
			</p>
			<p>
				Registering to vote turns a passive, invisible voter into an active and accounted-for participant in the electoral process. In doing so, the diaspora not only exercises its right but also protects its identity from being misused.
			</p>
			<p>
				Voting rights are not only protected by voting, but also by refusing to passively support fraudulent elections. An active diaspora is a political force. An invisible diaspora is a resource in the hands of others.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="w-full mt-6">
			<h2 class="title mb-4 text-xl text-accent-two">Before the elections are announced</h2>

			<h3 class="title mb-2 text-l text-accent-three">Voting eligibility</h3>
			<p>
				Citizens of Serbia with valid ID or passport are eligible to vote. If your passport has expired, you must apply for a new one at the nearest consulate.
			</p>
			<p>
				More info: <a href="https://www.mfa.gov.rs/gradjani/usluge/putne-isprave" target="_blank">mfa.gov.rs</a>
			</p>

			<h3 class="title mb-2 text-l text-accent-three">Check the electoral roll</h3>
			<p>
				You must be registered to vote. Check your status at: <a href="https://upit.birackispisak.gov.rs" target="_blank">upit.birackispisak.gov.rs</a>
			</p>
			<p>
				If not listed, you can register only after elections are announced.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="w-full mt-6">
			<h2 class="title mb-4 text-xl text-accent-two">After elections are announced</h2>

			<h3 class="title mb-2 text-l text-accent-three">Registering in the electoral roll</h3>
			<p>
				If you're not already registered, you must submit a request at least five days before the roll is finalized.
			</p>

			<h3 class="title mb-2 text-l text-accent-three">Voting from abroad</h3>
			<p>
				You must submit a request to vote from abroad regardless of previous participation. See the Law on the Unified Electoral Roll for details.
			</p>

			<h3 class="title mb-2 text-l text-accent-three">Request for voter information</h3>
			<p>
				It’s highly recommended to email the consulate requesting confirmation of your registration, even though it's not legally required.
			</p>

			<h3 class="title mb-2 text-l text-accent-three">Follow up on requests</h3>
			<p>
				Make sure your request was received by contacting the consulate (email, phone, or in person).
			</p>

			<h3 class="title mb-2 text-l text-accent-three">Polling station determination</h3>
			<p>
				Polling stations are formed for 100–2,500 voters (with exceptions allowed by the RIK).
			</p>
			<p>
				Forms: <a href="https://www.eupropisi.com/dokumenti/SG_091_2023_002.docx" target="_blank">Official template</a>
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="w-full mt-6">
			<h2 class="title mb-4 text-xl text-accent-two">On election day</h2>

			<h3 class="title mb-2 text-l text-accent-three">How to report irregularities</h3>
			<ul class="list-inside list-disc list-content" role="list">
				<li>Campaign materials near polling station</li>
				<li>Voting without proper ID</li>
				<li>Pressure by polling board members</li>
				<li>Unmarked voter lists or tampering</li>
				<li>Police presence without cause</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Request all irregularities to be noted in the official record.
			</p>
			<p>
				You can report within 24 hours. More info: <a href="https://www.cesid.rs/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Vodi%C4%8D-za-za%C5%A1titu-izbornog-prava.pdf" target="_blank">CeSID Guide</a>
			</p>
		</section>
	</article>

</BaseLayout>